+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+On the adversarial synthetic corpus with a 30-word vocabulary, the measured
+full-recall p95 for the `UserPromptSubmit` hook was **10.27 ms** before the
+term-selection fix.
+
+The fix discarded query terms whose document frequency was greater than one
+third of the corpus (`df > n / 3`), avoiding long posting-list scans for terms
+that carried little signal. The synthetic benchmark corpus was also changed to
+a Zipf-shaped vocabulary (30 frequent domain words plus rare identifiers), so
+the post-fix result includes both the term-selection correction and the more
+realistic corpus distribution.
+
+After those changes, the measured full-recall p95 was **1.82 ms**.
